## Summary

Saving a scene that contains a mesh to a `.glb` path throws `RangeError [ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE]` and writes no file. The JSON form (`.gltf`) of the same scene is written. `GltfSaveOptions.binaryMode = true` fails the same way.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux)
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

const scene = new Scene();
scene.rootNode.createChildNode('n', triangle());

scene.save('out.gltf');
console.log('out.gltf written:', fs.existsSync('out.gltf'));

scene.save('out.glb');
```

## Expected

`out.glb` is written and can be read back by `Scene.open`.

## Actual result

```
out.gltf written: true
RangeError [ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE]: The value of "offset" is out of range. It must be >= 0 and <= 632. Received 636
    at GltfExporter._writeGlb (dist/aspose/threed/formats/gltf/GltfExporter.js:319)
```
The existing test `TestGltfExporter > testSimpleTriangleBinary` fails with the same error.

## Where in the repository

- `src/aspose/threed/formats/gltf/GltfExporter.ts:418-420`: `_writeGlb` writes every entry of `binaryBuffer` with `writeFloatLE(binaryBuffer[i], offset); offset += 4;`
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/gltf/GltfExporter.ts:103,115`: `binaryBuffer` is a `number[]` and `buffers[0].byteLength` is `binaryBuffer.length`, so the BIN chunk is allocated for one byte per entry while the loop advances four
- `tests/test_gltf_exporter.test.ts` (`testSimpleTriangleBinary`)

